  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Define \\(a@b = ab - b^2\\) and \\(a\\#b = a + b - ab^2.\\) What is \\[\\dfrac{6@2}{6\\#2}?\\]",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-\\dfrac{1}{4}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{8}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{4}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "-1/2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2007-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The numerator is \\(6@2 = 6 \\cdot 2 - 2^2 = 12 - 4 = 8.\\)\n\nThe denominator is \\(6\\#2 = 6 + 2 - 6 \\cdot 2^2\\) \\(= 8 - 24\\) \\(= -16.\\)\n\nThe quotient is \\[ \\dfrac{8}{-16} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Substitute \\(a = 6\\) and \\(b = 2\\) into each definition",
        "The numerator is \\(6 \\cdot 2 - 2^2\\) and the denominator is \\(6 + 2 - 6 \\cdot 2^2\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
